00:34:09.640 --> 00:34:12.380
Yet again, it's doing
interesting things in the brain,

00:34:12.380 --> 00:34:15.900
and I think it does have something to do

00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:18.140
with the oxidative
stress, the glutathione,

00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:20.803
which would be relevant for TBI treatment.

00:34:21.670 --> 00:34:23.523
It hasn't been shown empirically

00:34:23.523 --> 00:34:25.210
that that helps with treatment,

00:34:25.210 --> 00:34:28.253
but I do think someone
could do that study.

00:34:29.330 --> 00:34:31.810
I think that it should be done, honestly,

00:34:31.810 --> 00:34:33.230
because it's a low-hanging fruit,

00:34:33.230 --> 00:34:34.840
I mean, if there's any impact.

00:34:34.840 --> 00:34:36.893
And there is at least
one preliminary study

00:34:36.893 --> 00:34:39.060
that glutathione is increased in the brain

00:34:39.060 --> 00:34:42.483
after humans are basically
taking sulforaphane.

00:34:43.580 --> 00:34:45.160
- Which is, really, for people listening,

00:34:45.160 --> 00:34:47.310
that's so important because
a number of compounds

00:34:47.310 --> 00:34:49.060
that people take in supplement form

00:34:49.060 --> 00:34:50.910
don't cross the blood-brain barrier,

00:34:50.910 --> 00:34:52.600
or they get metabolized in ways

00:34:52.600 --> 00:34:55.230
that what's listed on the
bottle almost becomes irrelevant

00:34:55.230 --> 00:34:57.410
for what your cells actually experience.

00:34:57.410 --> 00:34:59.430
So that's very reassuring.

