marine types of animals,

00:35:45.470 --> 00:35:47.760
fish, cold water fish, fatty fish.

00:35:47.760 --> 00:35:49.960
So there's three fatty acids.

00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:51.790
There's one from a plant,

00:35:51.790 --> 00:35:55.050
and that's often referred to
as ALA, people call it short,

00:35:55.050 --> 00:35:56.520
alpha-linolenic acid,

00:35:56.520 --> 00:35:59.770
and then there's
eicosapentaenoic acid, or EPA,

00:35:59.770 --> 00:36:02.320
and docosahexaenoic acid, which is DHA.

00:36:02.320 --> 00:36:03.830
Yeah, but EPA-
- I'm amazed you can pronounce

00:36:03.830 --> 00:36:07.920
two of the most difficult
words to pronounce and spell

00:36:07.920 --> 00:36:09.190
right next to ophthalmology,

00:36:09.190 --> 00:36:10.630
which, if you can spell it.

