in the actual supplement,

00:46:30.510 --> 00:46:33.830
because nothing is ever
what it says on the bottle,

00:46:33.830 --> 00:46:36.670
and then they also measure contaminants,

00:46:36.670 --> 00:46:39.010
so mercury, PCBs, dioxins,

00:46:39.010 --> 00:46:41.400
things that you'd find potentially in fish

00:46:41.400 --> 00:46:43.030
that are harmful to humans,

00:46:43.030 --> 00:46:47.620
and they also measure mercury
and then oxidized fatty acids.

00:46:47.620 --> 00:46:49.540
So these omega-3 fatty acids

00:46:49.540 --> 00:46:51.780
are polyunsaturated fatty acids,

00:46:51.780 --> 00:46:54.400
which are extremely prone to oxidation.

00:46:54.400 --> 00:46:57.420
So please keep your fish
oil in the refrigerator

00:46:57.420 --> 00:46:58.450
