00:46:58.450 --> 00:47:00.500
Yeah, they're extremely prone.
- Mine's in the cupboard,

00:47:00.500 --> 00:47:01.376
so now I know.

00:47:01.376 --> 00:47:05.590
- The shelf life's
increased. Lower oxidation.

00:47:05.590 --> 00:47:07.730
- No, it makes perfect sense. Yeah.

00:47:07.730 --> 00:47:10.450
- So, anyways, they measure that.

00:47:10.450 --> 00:47:12.210
And I typically like to look for,

00:47:12.210 --> 00:47:13.960
they give you a total oxidation number.

00:47:13.960 --> 00:47:17.260
It's called T-O-T-O-X.

00:47:17.260 --> 00:47:19.240
TOTOX is what we call it for short.

00:47:19.240 --> 00:47:22.690
And I like it to be at the least under 10,

00:47:22.690 --> 00:47:23.580
ideally under six.

00:47:23.580 --> 00:47:26.830
It's really hard to find all
