00:49:49.610 --> 00:49:52.963
But, so, within that paper,

00:49:53.970 --> 00:49:55.186
doing background research,

00:49:55.186 --> 00:49:56.240
and this was a review article, by the way,

00:49:56.240 --> 00:49:58.060
I was just connecting dots
'cause I love doing that.

00:49:58.060 --> 00:49:59.068
- I'm going to grab that paper.

00:49:59.068 --> 00:50:00.550
I confess, I don't know the paper,

00:50:00.550 --> 00:50:03.450
but I love quality reviews

00:50:03.450 --> 00:50:06.120
because the references
they're in are so useful.

00:50:06.120 --> 00:50:09.590
- Well, there's a huge
role for inflammation,

00:50:09.590 --> 00:50:11.570
the cause of inflammation in depression.

00:50:11.570 --> 00:50:15.050
And I think we did a short
animated video on this as well,

00:50:15.050 --> 00:50:18.230
years ago, back when I
was publishing that work,

00:50:18.230 --> 00:50:22.480
where people are injected
with lipopolysaccharide.

00:50:22.480 --> 00:50:26.060
This is something that we're
generating from our gut,

00:50:26.060 --> 00:50:30.701
mostly from our gut permeability,
which happens a lot.

00:50:30.701 --> 00:50:32.703
Endotoxin, it's also called.

00:50:32.703 --> 00:50:34.179
It's endotoxin lipopolysaccharide.

00:50:34.179 --> 00:50:37.030
It's basically the outer
membrane of bacterial cells

00:50:37.030 --> 00:50:40.200
when bacteria die, so like when
the immune cells in our gut

00:50:40.200 --> 00:50:42.150
come into contact with the bacteria

00:50:42.150 --> 00:50:46.333
because we drank alcohol five
days in a row or whatever,

00:50:47.290 --> 00:50:49.890
we release endotoxin, or
something stressed us out.

00:50:49.890 --> 00:50:51.610
We release endotoxin into our body,

00:50:51.610 --> 00:50:53.127
and that causes inflammation.

00:50:53.127 --> 00:50:56.750
And so you can inject people
with lipopolysaccharide

00:50:56.750 --> 00:50:58.770
and cause depressive symptoms.

00:50:58.770 --> 00:51:01.640
However, if you take those
same cohort of people,

00:51:01.640 --> 00:51:02.740
give them EPA,

00:51:02.740 --> 00:51:04.820
and I think it was
somewhere around two grams,

00:51:04.820 --> 00:51:06.590
and then inject them
with lipopolysaccharide.

00:51:06.590 --> 00:51:09.000
We're establishing causation here, right?

00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:11.440
It totally, the depressive
symptoms, versus a placebo.

00:51:11.440 --> 00:51:13.460
So the placebo was saline control.

00:51:13.460 --> 00:51:14.980
So this was a placebo controlled

00:51:14.980 --> 00:51:18.000
because obviously it's hugely
important for depression.

00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:20.080
It ameliorated the depressive symptoms

00:51:20.080 --> 00:51:21.800
that was caused by lipopolysaccharide.

00:51:21.800 --> 00:51:25.830
- Amazing, and LPS,
lipopolysaccharide, is no joke.

00:51:25.830 --> 00:51:28.430
Years ago, when I was working
on thermal regulation,

00:51:29.880 --> 00:51:33.173
we would inject animals
with LPS to induce fever.

00:51:34.317 --> 00:51:37.560
The vagus nerve registers
the presence of LPS signals

00:51:37.560 --> 00:51:40.560
to these particular hyperglycemic areas

00:51:40.560 --> 00:51:41.790
and cranks up body temperature

00:51:41.790 --> 00:51:44.790
because, basically, it's a
signal that the body is infected.

00:51:46.450 --> 00:51:47.710
Amazing.

00:51:47.710 --> 00:51:50.990
So I will continue with
my two grams per day.

00:51:50.990 --> 00:51:52.440
Maybe I'll ramp it up to four.

00:51:52.440 --> 00:51:55.650
I'm not doing the DHA separately.

