02:07:11.930 --> 02:07:14.190
of mitochondrial biogenesis
in their muscle tissue,

02:07:14.190 --> 02:07:17.550
and the amount of mitochondrial biogenesis

02:07:17.550 --> 02:07:19.060
in old people specifically,

02:07:19.060 --> 02:07:20.820
it happened in both
young and old from HIT,

02:07:20.820 --> 02:07:22.530
from the high-intensity interval training,

02:07:22.530 --> 02:07:25.000
was, I mean, it was enormous,

02:07:25.000 --> 02:07:27.000
at least 50%, I think.

02:07:27.000 --> 02:07:29.040
- [Andrew] Fantastic.
- So it was just like, whoa!

02:07:29.040 --> 02:07:30.751
And so, why would you want that?

02:07:30.751 --> 02:07:32.713
Well, mitochondria,

02:07:34.238 --> 02:07:35.770
your cells are turning over.

02:07:35.770 --> 02:07:37.467
You make new cells. You replace old ones.

02:07:37.467 --> 02:07:39.000
With your mitochondria,

02:07:39.000 --> 02:07:41.130
you don't really do
that for the most part.

02:07:41.130 --> 02:07:41.963
You can.

02:07:41.963 --> 02:07:43.120
Mitochondrial biogenesis does happen,

02:07:43.120 --> 02:07:45.130
but you have to stimulate it to happen.

02:07:45.130 --> 02:07:48.180
And what happens with your mitochondria

02:07:48.180 --> 02:07:50.600
is they essentially are bobbing
around inside of your cells,

02:07:50.600 --> 02:07:53.170
and then they fuse with
other mitochondria,

02:07:53.170 --> 02:07:55.660
exchange all their
content, mitochondrial DNA,

02:07:55.660 --> 02:07:56.530
and then fizz back apart.

02:07:56.530 --> 02:07:58.780
And that's how they
kind of stay young-ish.

02:07:58.780 --> 02:08:00.773
But, as you age, you keep doing that

02:08:00.773 --> 02:08:02.630
with the same pool of mitochondria,

02:08:02.630 --> 02:08:04.240
then you're going to get a
bunch of old mitochondria

02:08:04.240 --> 02:08:06.180
mixing old stuff together, right?

02:08:06.180 --> 02:08:10.280
So, why wouldn't you want
to bring up new, healthy,

02:08:10.280 --> 02:08:13.440
young mitochondria into that pool, right?

02:08:13.440 --> 02:08:16.120
So, in my mind, when I hear
mitochondrial biogenesis,

02:08:16.120 --> 02:08:17.430
I'm like, aging.

02:08:17.430 --> 02:08:19.200
That's the first thing I think of.

02:08:19.200 --> 02:08:21.650
So, anyways, cold exposure does that.

02:08:21.650 --> 02:08:23.120
