02:45:11.210 --> 02:45:12.060
I do sweat a lot,

02:45:12.060 --> 02:45:13.387
and that's another thing
we didn't talk about.

02:45:13.387 --> 02:45:15.530
You do sweat some heavy metals.

02:45:15.530 --> 02:45:19.900
And some heavy metals are
excreted predominantly

02:45:19.900 --> 02:45:22.290
through sweat and others through urine.

02:45:22.290 --> 02:45:24.960
So, for example, cadmium,

02:45:24.960 --> 02:45:26.880
there's like a 125-fold increase

02:45:26.880 --> 02:45:30.610
in cadmium excretion from sweat
when you get in the sauna.

02:45:30.610 --> 02:45:34.710
Also, lead is something like
17-fold excretions higher.

02:45:34.710 --> 02:45:37.180
Another one is aluminum.
It's about fourfold higher.

02:45:37.180 --> 02:45:39.580
So infrared, you do sweat a lot too,

02:45:39.580 --> 02:45:41.260
and that's because the main difference

02:45:41.260 --> 02:45:43.680
is that you're heating your body up

02:45:43.680 --> 02:45:48.220
through thermal radiation
versus the ambient air.

02:45:48.220 --> 02:45:50.838
A standard sauna is a heater,

02:45:50.838 --> 02:45:52.300
and the heater's heating up the air,

02:45:52.300 --> 02:45:54.490
and that's how you're heating yourself up.

02:45:54.490 --> 02:45:56.440
So it is a little bit of
a different mechanism.

02:45:56.440 --> 02:45:58.460
I prefer regular saunas.

02:45:58.460 --> 02:46:01.470
Most of the data out there is
from the heat stress itself.

02:46:01.470 --> 02:46:03.730
